      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Hello, it sounds like you're wearing a particularly small avatar!\nSmall avatars might have limbs short enough that you'll encounter \"near-plane culling\", which is basically a phrase describing a distance that the camera won't render anything closer than that. It's controlled by the world author's settings in the reference camera.\nSmall avatars will run into this more often, especially ones with viewpoints out farther from the head bone (aka: you have a big head). \nYou can mitigate this by using a taller avatar, or by moving your viewpoint closer in to the head bone. This can cause other problems, but it's a tradeoff.\nIn short: not a bug, normal Unity behavior!",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
